Z||000000||2birds||02-19-2001||09:08 PM||||I just drove a 91 Mustang GT and a 95 Z-28, both convertibles, today.  I was amazed by how floppy the bodies felt when hitting rough sections of the road.  Are all unibody convertibles that bad, or did I just run across a bad pair? <BR>BTW, I'm in the market for one or the other, so any info on either, good or bad, is apppreciated.  I'm pretty knowledgable on Fords (I think), but the 93 and up F-bodies are new to me.  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Pontiaddict||02-19-2001||11:08 PM||||Some are better than others, but they are all usually bad. They should make subframe connectors mandatory on them. It gives you a good reason to put in a roll bar though.||||reg||1
Z||000002||My7Fieros||02-20-2001||03:11 AM||||Mustang covt's didnt have cross members until.....(sigh) lemme think, I used to really be into Mustangs...I believe, it wasnt until the 99 models came out..but may have been 97 or 98. At any rate, the one you drove didnt..wasnt (for sure) until the sn94 body styles.............||||reg||1
Z||000003||2birds||02-20-2001||04:59 PM||||My old Super Ford issues say it was the 94-up bodies that got some real bracing for the Mustang convertibles.  Haven't driven one of those yet.  I drove a 93 GT ragtop a long time ago, and it was real floppy, too.<BR>The Camaro was like night and day different over the Mustang.  Both were automatics, and Ford's AOD really sucked back then, before the electronic versions came out.  GM always seemed to have the 700-R4/4L60E trannies right.  The Z28 had tons of bottom end torque, too.  The interior felt much more modern, too, with a fully lined top and nicer seats and controls.<P>I'm mainly trying to figure out what kind of problems these things had, and what to stay away from.  The Z28 bulletin board I found had many times more archives to search through than this one.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Slammed Fiero||02-21-2001||12:03 AM||||We have a 95 Convert 5.0ltr mustang. The car is tight after 5 years , which is less than I can say for the 94 Camaro Z28 we had , we sold it in 98 , We bought it new, after about 2 years it creaked and groaned. Had lotsa power , but the fit and finish on the mustang is far better , the ride is far smoother. I'm a GM man through and through , but the mustang is a better car. The camaro was a coupe auto , the mustang is a convert with the auto , and the Ultra rare fiberglass hardtop ..still in the crate.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan M McCreery<BR>86 GT<BR>New Custom White face gauges 17" Tr motorsports Typhoons Ground Control coil overs , Big bars front and rear , Mustang scoop , accel coil , no cat , 4spd , short shift , poly dog bone and bushings momo pedals and shift knob , round headlight conversion , Geni stainless steel oval exhaust tips. Pioneer 6000 CD player , Sony Mobile Amp. Currently doing big brake conversion...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/jssig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
